#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275126 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184149 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84355770-5926-5be6-9b9f-c13bb05599ae" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Horizontal Shift of a Horizontally Stretched Tangent or Cotangent Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27dd6c2e-56f6-5224-a92d-a900e47fbf5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272740} {:answer/id #uuid "4d20665a-d072-5d38-bc2e-83cd6ab4dfd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273035} {:answer/id #uuid "69b8a942-cc3f-5887-9b9a-88358ec6410d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273298} {:answer/id #uuid "a7e2122f-6484-54b6-b0a8-b983751ab3ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273841} {:answer/id #uuid "dc531f8c-0ec3-5820-905b-629562f0fa99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27dd6c2e-56f6-5224-a92d-a900e47fbf5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272740} :answer-field/id #uuid "b21fc2a6-944a-50a1-a0fa-69bde4da9e7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274944}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bdfc61bf-0fdc-5699-9c08-0b5a229a8b71" :question/math-academy-id "q-143670" :question/problem "![](images/c2/c2e5b01cf03f1f9d82562ee51fc484448e90b74dd2584daf18a499849ca36bff.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}+C),$ where $C$ is a constant. Given that $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ what is the value of $C?$" :question/worked-solution "The parameter $C$ represents a horizontal shift of the function.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the function by factoring the horizontal stretch factor, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}+C) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{1}{3}(x+3C))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $x+3C$ indicates that the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{1}{3}(x+3C))$ is a horizontal translation of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}).$ Comparing the two graphs below allows us to determine the amount of this shift.\n\n![](images/29/29346a073d6a22f0bab74eeac86431e8c761c9ed21a005ec6965f71e6436c117.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that our curve has been obtained by shifting $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})$ by $\\frac{7\\pi }{4}-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ units to the right. Therefore:\n\n$$\n3C=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,⟹\\,C=-\\frac{\\pi }{12}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ is in this interval, the value of $C$ is $-\\frac{\\pi }{12}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275128 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184149 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84355770-5926-5be6-9b9f-c13bb05599ae" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Horizontal Shift of a Horizontally Stretched Tangent or Cotangent Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fb8c6d5-62f2-5f9e-9dff-a6c6cf210773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272526} {:answer/id #uuid "3d8111fb-6012-56e0-a9b6-3275417d9a31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272916} {:answer/id #uuid "8340b495-0e27-5ab2-8265-89b8a8f42f44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273514} {:answer/id #uuid "ceceedd5-348a-5f86-9a42-9b4e036292b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274185} {:answer/id #uuid "ed397ac8-10b1-54c0-9046-d661bdad85ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d8111fb-6012-56e0-a9b6-3275417d9a31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272916} :answer-field/id #uuid "b42dc950-3ab6-53ee-bb79-c0cd1d57e61e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274946}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "587d6141-4c7d-5ff0-9ea2-3cc64d30a411" :question/math-academy-id "q-143672" :question/problem "![](images/6a/6a90f799d2dfd2dbd971e15eb195f4109ab7b6ceb204943a8ed2fd6c83bb620c.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+C),$ where $C$ is a constant. Given that $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ what is the value of $C?$" :question/worked-solution "The parameter $C$ represents a horizontal shift of the function.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the function by factoring the horizontal stretch factor, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+C) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}(x+2C))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $x+2C$ indicates that the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}(x+2C))$ is a horizontal translation of $y=cot\\,(\\frac{x}{2}).$ Comparing the two graphs below allows us to determine the amount of this shift.\n\n![](images/0e/0e94fbec60ae4d47d3a4fba50f8a875d9bb3938776940cc9688413d2cb22aa9e.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that our curve has been obtained by shifting $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})$ by $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ units to the left. Therefore:\n\n$$\n2C=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,⟹\\,C=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275132 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184149 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84355770-5926-5be6-9b9f-c13bb05599ae" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Horizontal Shift of a Horizontally Stretched Tangent or Cotangent Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38f5df54-de20-581a-a052-687662bac099" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272886} {:answer/id #uuid "59ea7cd8-2c89-5af6-9951-0c58c07e0a6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273157} {:answer/id #uuid "98bf869f-24f8-50f3-ac5e-4060bb11e000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273712} {:answer/id #uuid "b3d9faeb-5941-52e8-928f-04d747d92a64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273945} {:answer/id #uuid "c58db38f-c8f1-5754-b80e-2298972c7447" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59ea7cd8-2c89-5af6-9951-0c58c07e0a6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273157} :answer-field/id #uuid "20a99701-dbbe-534f-a0ce-166bf09e58cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274695}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7239e789-03d0-5ec3-8e95-e5eb72761b2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-143677" :question/problem "![](images/76/7602d1695610361f28613d8bf3542056b2624f9b6b8980873f6fdebf802c6750.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3}+C),$ where $C$ is a constant. Given that $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ what is the value of $C?$" :question/worked-solution "The parameter $C$ represents a horizontal shift of the function.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the function by factoring the horizontal stretch factor, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3}+C) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}(x+\\frac{3C}{2}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $x+\\frac{3C}{2}$ indicates that the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}(x+\\frac{3C}{2}))$ is a horizontal translation of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3}).$ Comparing the two graphs below allows us to determine the amount of this shift.\n\n![](images/01/015ca9336646a7545de842414ace2c2a695688e30653b2ed019000d69609d56d.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that our curve has been obtained by shifting $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3})$ by $\\frac{3\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ units to the left. Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3C}{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,⟹\\,C=(\\frac{\\pi }{4})(\\frac{2}{3})\\,⟹\\,C=\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is in this interval, the value of $C$ is $\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275149 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068825 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc419917-fe34-5bf9-8bf0-1b022fce11ff" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a \"Less Than\" Inequality Given the Graph of the Corresponding Parabola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f130433-4070-55a2-99e0-a86650ea2a06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x<0$ or $x>20$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272521} {:answer/id #uuid "18cd1907-4fdd-5d24-8647-8429844e6c6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<x<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272602} {:answer/id #uuid "53664bf7-6f85-59d9-b6e9-c20637f1d94c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2<x<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273097} {:answer/id #uuid "8b6a31bf-791b-5b3d-94f3-7d052755115e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x<-2$ or $x>0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273590} {:answer/id #uuid "d3fb79e4-b4cd-5b93-8f16-b66659212867" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2<x<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274244}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53664bf7-6f85-59d9-b6e9-c20637f1d94c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2<x<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273097} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c71f562-d7b0-53b0-8040-be0d728bcb1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274713}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b5ba8619-41db-5874-87c3-131cea1a0aff" :question/math-academy-id "q-144414" :question/problem "![](images/4e/4e36490c5c66b0dc463e9729cc494964b9501e8571b213761f3f029863331b3e.png)\n\nGiven the graph above, solve the inequality $x(x+2)<0.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\nx(x+2)<0\n$$\n\n \n\nis a \"*less than*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=x(x+2)\n$$\n\nis *below *the $x$-axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/45/45ecefb7d229f6882bc4e5cd4b3583e65a295c83cdd4de83d9d8fa3719e33b54.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $-2<x<0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396066 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078391 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "98e3f3b4-8dfa-515c-90b1-09fb19d68144" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center and Radius of a Circle by Completing the Square with Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2fe06dc-0609-5053-9367-73d7ebf2fcb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "center: $(-2,-2)$, radius: $\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{2}}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396068} {:answer/id #uuid "3f353887-7ced-5107-882a-0276e72dd462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "center: $(-2,2)$, radius: $\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{2}}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396069} {:answer/id #uuid "d0c03ddb-5aef-510c-adf3-fa2a8970e245" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "center: $(2,2)$, radius: $\\frac{13}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396070} {:answer/id #uuid "ef5518f9-14b3-5d56-ae49-14acc285d236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "center: $(2,4)$, radius: $\\frac{13}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396071} {:answer/id #uuid "0ddf99ec-bda7-505b-b4fe-67ffc75b34aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "center: $(2,-2)$, radius: $\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{2}}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ddf99ec-bda7-505b-b4fe-67ffc75b34aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "center: $(2,-2)$, radius: $\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{2}}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396072} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bd2771d-4f88-578f-9fd3-675729a93312" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0485f61e-5d32-5461-91b2-4119de37bba9" :question/math-academy-id "q-14619" :question/problem "Find the radius and center of the circle whose equation is\n$2{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-8x+8y+3=0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-8x+8y+3 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4x+4y & =-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-4x)+({y}^{2}+4y) & =-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2})+({y}^{2}+2\\cdot 2y+{2}^{2}) & =-\\frac{3}{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+4)+({y}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+4) & =\\frac{13}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect square and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+{(y+2)}^{2} & =\\frac{13}{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+{(y-(-2))}^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{2}})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(2,-2)$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{2}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060060 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059852 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82f31c6e-f9df-5e0a-88a4-a8ccfca00258" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product of Two Parallel Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f27867c-9451-52d4-9675-56489e7ec374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272522} {:answer/id #uuid "21cb1b31-bd6b-5005-a1c7-224eb791a510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272688} {:answer/id #uuid "28a3f458-1cec-5fd4-b797-aa052f1583df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272746} {:answer/id #uuid "90858102-719e-537c-b0af-d447bb858e94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273645} {:answer/id #uuid "cee5ad2a-4949-58a7-a470-aefe6d88d424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90858102-719e-537c-b0af-d447bb858e94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273645} :answer-field/id #uuid "931ce724-c38c-5e87-8825-093612bce144" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "57870dea-e562-5a28-b808-03713548edd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-146263" :question/problem "The vector $a$ has magnitude $3,$ the vector $b$ has magnitude $4,$ and the angle between the vectors is ${0}^{∘}.$ What is $a\\times b?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $a$ and $b$ are nonzero vectors. Then, $a\\times b=0$ if and only if $a∥b.$\n\nSince the angle between $a$ and $b$ is ${0}^{∘},$ our vectors must be parallel. \n\nTherefore, $a\\times b=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275161 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059852 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82f31c6e-f9df-5e0a-88a4-a8ccfca00258" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product of Two Parallel Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0082e7c0-3530-59f2-ba9a-26fd87e6a277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272389} {:answer/id #uuid "301e0cb5-f0c5-55af-95b8-6ed70646dde2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272816} {:answer/id #uuid "350e615d-c623-5564-ac9d-ffb3c30557ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592